// =============================================================================
// Old Pell — Lumbermill.  Questline: "Roots Run Deep" (vendor.lumbermill)
// Keystone: the Heartwood Sapling.  Teaches harvest sites + terrain restoration.
// =============================================================================
title: TalkToLumbermill
---
<<if $q_lumber_stage == 0>>
    Old Pell: Used to be I'd fell a tree and two'd grow back. Now the wood comes up grey. The forest's sick, same as the Heart.
    -> Can I help the grove?
        Old Pell: Clear the blight off my old grove in the Verdant Forest and I'll get the saws singing again.
        <<set $q_lumber_stage = 1>>
        <<command: StartQuest vendor.lumbermill>>
        Old Pell: "Roots Run Deep," my grandmother called it. Go on, then.
    -> Just trade wood.
        <<command: OpenShop "lumbermill">>
<<elseif $q_lumber_stage == 1>>
    Old Pell: Is the grove cleared of the grey rot?
    -> The grove's clean.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.lumbermill>>
        <<set $q_lumber_stage = 2>>
        Old Pell: Saws are singing again, hear that? Now — carry a sapling from the Heart of Elarion and plant it in the bare patch. New roots from the old.
    -> Not yet.
        Old Pell: Grey wood splinters wrong. Mind your hands out there.
<<elseif $q_lumber_stage == 2>>
    Old Pell: Did you plant the Heart's sapling?
    -> It's in the ground.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.lumbermill>>
        <<set $q_lumber_stage = 3>>
        Old Pell: Then guard it through the night-raid. Young roots don't survive an orc's torch alone.
    -> Not yet.
        Old Pell: Carry it gentle. That sapling's a piece of the Heart itself.
<<elseif $q_lumber_stage == 3>>
    Old Pell: Did the sapling live through the night?
    -> It stands.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.lumbermill>>
        <<command: GiveKeystone "HeartwoodSapling">>
        <<set $q_lumber_stage = 9>>
        Old Pell: Then take the Heartwood Sapling, and my thanks. The saws run faster now, and the forest's coming back green where you walked. Mother Wren'll want to hear it — full forests make full fields.
    -> Not yet.
        Old Pell: Don't let it burn. Go.
<<else>>
    Old Pell: The Heartwood-bearer. The grove's yours as much as mine now. What'll you have?
    -> Trade wood.
        <<command: OpenShop "lumbermill">>
    -> Upgrade the lumbermill.
        <<command: OpenUpgrade "lumbermill">>
    -> Nothing today.
        Old Pell: Mind the saplings.
<<endif>>
===
